title: Shape, built in Shape
theme: midnight

try: Try it — double-click Roadmap · the round button is AI · right-click anything [sticky, yellow, x: 860, y: 250]


mindmap goal: Bring ../schema onto the board [x: 0, y: 70] {
  Why
    Data models live in ../schema
  Steps
    Wrap schema-core
    Draw it like ../schema
  Done when [green]
    A schema diffs by column
}

kanban week: This week [x: -10, y: 300] {
  column todo: To do {
    schema: Schema block [owner: deyan]
  }
  column doing: Doing {
    site: Landing page [blue, owner: claude]
  }
  column done: Done {
    todos: To-do lists [green]
  }
}

group inside: Boards inside this board [x: 690, y: 10] {
  plan-link: Roadmap [pill, blue, canvas: plan]
  data-link: Data model [canvas: data, detail: ER · crow's feet]
  flow-link: How AI edits a board [rounded, purple, canvas: flow]
  metrics-link: Releases [text, canvas: metrics]
}

comment on goal by deyan: Should schemas get their own perspective?
reply c1 by mia: Start in Delivery; see the decision in Roadmap.

canvas plan: Roadmap {
  gantt next: What's next [start: 2026-10-17] {
    To-do lists [2d, owner: deyan, done]
    Schema block [2w, after: to-do-lists, done: 40%]
    Linux window [1w, after: to-do-lists, orange]
    Shape 1.0 [after: schema-block linux-window, milestone, green]
  }

  risks shape: Risks {
    AI CLIs change their flags [p: 3, i: 4, owner: deyan]
    Scope creep, again [p: 3, i: 5]
    Big boards get slow [p: 3, i: 3]
  }

  adr git: Git is the database [accepted] {
    context: Boards should diff, review and merge like code.
    decision: One text file per board; collaboration is commits and pull requests.
  }
}

canvas data: Data model {
  entity boards: Boards {
    path:  text [pk]
    theme: text [null]
  }
  entity nodes: Nodes {
    id:    text [pk]
    board: text [fk: boards, rel: drawn on]
    label: text
  }
}

canvas flow: How AI edits a board {
  sequence ask: Ask the AI for a change {
    you: You [person]
    editor: Editor
    server: Local server
    ai: Your AI CLI [cloud]
    you -> editor: Add a Linux window
    editor -> server: POST /api/ai
    server -> ai: prompt on stdin
    ai ..> server: a few ops
    editor ..> you: Keep or discard?
  }
}

canvas metrics: Releases {
  layout: grid
  chart releases: Releases so far [line] {
    day    | Releases
    Oct 7  | 1
    Oct 12 | 22
    Oct 15 | 40
    Oct 18 | 76
    Oct 19 | 78
  }
  chart code: Code by part [donut, unit: %] {
    Core 71
    Editor 17
    CLI 10
    WASM 2
  }
}
